 "subject": "Get list of tip labels that are subset by node",
 "messages_listed": 2,
 "last_activity": "2019-05-29T02:48:19Z",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "cvO6DiYaAgAJ",
   "from": "Kurt Y",
   "author": "112a116ba16ec2aa",
   "date": "2019-05-28T22:18:50Z",
   "subject": "Get list of tip labels that are subset by node",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I am trying to process a huge tree, whereby I want to get a printout list/vector/df of a designated clade&#39;s tip labels that occur after a selected node, so I can use that list of taxa in each clade to subset other data, rather then having to type out a ton of tip labels in each clade. <div><br></div><div>I can subset the tree and identify specific clades with subset_tree, or groupClade, and get a visual of these groupings, but have been unable to figure out how to get a list. I see the groupings are stored in the tree object as attributes, but I haven&#39;t been successful at accessing them. </div><div><br></div><div>Any help would be great! </div><div><br></div><div>Thanks,</div><div>Kurt</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "wsmXXJWpAwAJ",
   "from": "Yu, Guangchuang",
   "author": "cec41188340e8212",
   "date": "2019-05-29T02:48:19Z",
   "subject": "Re: Get list of tip labels that are subset by node",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);background-color:rgb(248,248,248);border-radius:3px;display:inline\">as.phylo(tree_subset(huge_tree, node, levels_back=0))$tip.label</code> should works, see <a href=\"https://yulab-smu.github.io/treedata-book/chapter2.html#subset-node\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://yulab-smu.github.io/treedata-book/chapter2.html%23subset-node&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482269607000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3LLsPMEh-bOkiCO2YB_aCt\">https://yulab-smu.github.io/treedata-book/chapter2.html#subset-node</a>.</p></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">On Wed, May 29, 2019 at 6:18 AM Kurt Y <a href=\"http://mailto:kur...@gmail.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://mailto:kur...@gmail.com&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482269608000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2BXdvk2HhQ1TbRlastufLz\">kurtyak...@gmail.com</a> wrote:</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\"></p></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">I am trying to process a huge tree, whereby I want to get a printout list/vector/df of a designated clade&#39;s tip labels that occur after a selected node, so I can use that list of taxa in each clade to subset other data, rather then having to type out a ton of tip labels in each clade. <div><br></div><div>I can subset the tree and identify specific clades with subset_tree, or groupClade, and get a visual of these groupings, but have been unable to figure out how to get a list. I see the groupings are stored in the tree object as attributes, but I haven&#39;t been successful at accessing them. </div><div><br></div><div>Any help would be great! </div><div><br></div><div>Thanks,</div><div>Kurt</div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
